// 原生书源引擎：链接了它，规则和 JavaScript 就由 legado-engine 跑；没有它
// 的平台（模拟器、Windows、Android、网页）这几条测试什么都不做。

import std/json

import ./sources

let nativeSample = r#"{"bookSourceUrl":"https://x.test","bookSourceName":"测试"}"#

test "the native engine runs a CSS rule" {
  if !sources.nativeAvailable() { return }
  let text = try sources.nativeEvalRule(nativeSample, ".row@text", "<div class='row'>Hello</div>", "https://x.test/")
  expect(text == "Hello")
}

test "the native engine runs a JavaScript rule" {
  if !sources.nativeAvailable() { return }
  let text = try sources.nativeEvalRule(nativeSample, "@js:result.trim().toUpperCase()", "hello", "https://x.test/")
  expect(text == "HELLO")
}

test "a source keeps the JSON it was imported from" {
  let one = r#"{"bookSourceName":"一个","bookSourceUrl":"x.test","searchUrl":"/s?q={{key}}","loginUrl":"/login"}"#
  let def = try sources.decodeSource(try json.parse(one))
  expect(def.raw.contains("\"loginUrl\""))
  expect(sources.sourceJSON(def) == def.raw)
}

test "the native engine turns chapter HTML into text" {
  if !sources.nativeAvailable() { return }
  let text = try sources.nativeEvalRule(nativeSample, "body", "<p>第一段</p><p>第二&amp;段</p>", "https://x.test/")
  expect(text.contains("第一段"))
  expect(text.contains("第二&段"))
  expect(!text.contains("<p>"))
}

test "a source's variables are what the engine stores, not the JSON's field" {
  if !sources.nativeAvailable() { return }
  let one = r#"{"bookSourceName":"变量","bookSourceUrl":"https://vars.test","variable":"{\"user\":\"from-json\"}"}"#
  let def = try sources.decodeSource(try sources.parseList(one)[0])
  // 引擎不读 JSON 里的 variable：导入时由 seedVariables 写，这里直接存一次。
  try await sources.saveVariables(def, r#"{"user":"a\"b","pass":"密码"}"#)
  let user = try await sources.nativeEval(sources.sourceJSON(def), script: "source.get('user')")
  let stored = try await sources.storedVariables(def)
  expect(user == "a\"b")
  expect(stored.contains("密码"))
}

test "a cookie the host sets is the source's session" {
  if !sources.nativeAvailable() { return }
  let one = r#"{"bookSourceUrl":"https://cookie.test"}"#
  let def = try sources.decodeSource(try sources.parseList(one)[0])
  try await sources.setCookieOf(def, url: "https://cookie.test/", cookie: "sid=abc; theme=dark")
  let header = try await sources.cookieHeaderOf(def, url: "https://cookie.test/page")
  expect(header.contains("sid=abc"))
  expect(header.contains("theme=dark"))
}
